\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {45}{\ignorespaces Intra-family consistency of DDR patterns. Each cell shows the mean Spearman $|\rho |$(depth, feature) across generators within a family ($\pm $ SD for multi-generator families). Drifting features exhibit consistently high $|\rho |$ while near-stationary features remain low across all families. $H_{\mathrm  {min}}$ is a \emph  {boundary feature}: its elevated $|\rho | \approx 0.40$ reflects a large gen-0$\to $gen-1 transition, whereas its Cohen's $d \approx 0$ for gen-1\,/\,gen-2+ confirms near-stationarity within the binary classification scope (\S  \ref {sec:results-differential}).}}{32}{table.caption.139}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:family_ddr_consistency}{{45}{32}{Intra-family consistency of DDR patterns. Each cell shows the mean Spearman $|\rho |$(depth, feature) across generators within a family ($\pm $ SD for multi-generator families). Drifting features exhibit consistently high $|\rho |$ while near-stationary features remain low across all families. $H_{\mathrm {min}}$ is a \emph {boundary feature}: its elevated $|\rho | \approx 0.40$ reflects a large gen-0$\to $gen-1 transition, whereas its Cohen's $d \approx 0$ for gen-1\,/\,gen-2+ confirms near-stationarity within the binary classification scope (\S \ref {sec:results-differential})}{table.caption.139}{}}
